WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.985
This is the introductory module of the Honest Polygon course.

2
00:00:03.985 --> 00:00:05.176
It has three topics:

3
00:00:05.176 --> 00:00:09.884
what the course gives and what it does not, why most trading ideas do not work,

4
00:00:09.884 --> 00:00:12.446
and how to read the numbers in the program.

5
00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.305
The program has two modes.

6
00:00:15.305 --> 00:00:16.949
Learning is the course:

7
00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:22.240
coins, exchanges, wallets, protocols, trading and honest testing of ideas.

8
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.170
Work is the testing itself:

9
00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:29.461
pick coins, choose an idea, test it on real history and watch it on paper,

10
00:00:29.461 --> 00:00:30.462
without money.

11
00:00:31.462 --> 00:00:33.654
This is what the work mode looks like.

12
00:00:33.654 --> 00:00:36.365
The wizard at the top tells you what to do now,

13
00:00:36.365 --> 00:00:39.595
why it matters and which mistake people make most often.

14
00:00:39.595 --> 00:00:42.190
The wizard forbids nothing; it only explains.

15
00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.923
The course gives understanding:

16
00:00:44.923 --> 00:00:49.282
what happens when you press “buy”, where the interest in protocols comes from,

17
00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:53.641
and why the same strategy looks brilliant on one stretch and fails on another.

18
00:00:53.641 --> 00:00:57.497
The course does not tell you what to buy and does not promise profit.

19
00:00:57.497 --> 00:00:59.174
This is not investment advice.

20
00:01:00.174 --> 00:01:03.727
Imagine ten people, each tossing a coin ten times.

21
00:01:03.727 --> 00:01:07.422
The best one usually gets six, seven or eight heads.

22
00:01:08.422 --> 00:01:13.102
Take a hundred people, and someone already has eight or nine heads out of ten,

23
00:01:13.102 --> 00:01:14.662
although the coin is fair.

24
00:01:15.662 --> 00:01:19.249
Five hundred people, and the best one looks like a master.

25
00:01:19.249 --> 00:01:20.300
But it is chance:

26
00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.217
there are simply many attempts.

27
00:01:22.217 --> 00:01:23.887
Trading ideas are the same.

28
00:01:23.887 --> 00:01:27.350
Test many ideas, and some will look excellent by chance.

29
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.649
That is why the program computes the t-statistic,

30
00:01:31.649 --> 00:01:37.304
how steadily the idea beat the benchmark, and compares it with the significance bar.

31
00:01:37.304 --> 00:01:40.131
The bar rises with the number of attempts:

32
00:01:40.131 --> 00:01:44.238
for one attempt it is 1.96, for five hundred it is about 3.5.

33
00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.829
The program is built on research:

34
00:01:47.829 --> 00:01:51.048
29 hypotheses and 563 variants on crypto.

35
00:01:51.048 --> 00:01:54.111
With that many attempts the bar is 3.1.

36
00:01:54.111 --> 00:01:58.822
Not one idea that predicts the direction of price passed it.

37
00:01:59.822 --> 00:02:00.841
Now the numbers.

38
00:02:00.841 --> 00:02:02.943
Every test has four main numbers.

39
00:02:02.943 --> 00:02:03.389
Return:

40
00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.746
how much the capital grew after fees.

41
00:02:05.746 --> 00:02:06.319
Drawdown:

42
00:02:06.319 --> 00:02:08.931
the deepest fall from a peak to a trough.

43
00:02:08.931 --> 00:02:13.262
It is what you will have to sit through without abandoning the idea.

44
00:02:14.262 --> 00:02:17.558
The third number is the comparison with the benchmark.

45
00:02:17.558 --> 00:02:22.319
Plus 80 percent means nothing if the coin rose 120 percent over the same time.

46
00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:25.371
The fourth is whether the result is above the bar.

47
00:02:25.371 --> 00:02:29.094
The program shows all of this side by side at the test stage.

48
00:02:30.094 --> 00:02:31.094
The main points.

49
00:02:31.094 --> 00:02:34.471
The course explains crypto and trading in plain words,

50
00:02:34.471 --> 00:02:38.098
and the program lets you check everything on real history.

51
00:02:38.098 --> 00:02:42.475
Almost all trading ideas, tested honestly, do not beat simple holding.

52
00:02:42.475 --> 00:02:44.788
Next come the lessons of this module:

53
00:02:44.788 --> 00:02:46.414
they are below this video.
